Translation patch: <HalfWidthScalar as TryFrom<Scalar>>::try_from (src/scalar.rs)

Change: `value.bytes[16..].iter().all(|&byte| byte == 0)` becomes a `while` loop over
the indices 16..32 that returns `Err(())` at the first nonzero byte, then `Ok(Self(value))`.

Why: Aeneas has no model of `Iterator::all` on slice iterators
(`core::slice::iter::Iter::all`), so the original leaves an undefined external
function in the translation.

Behaviour: identical. `all` checks bytes 16, 17, .., 31 in order and stops at the
first byte that is not zero; the loop does the same, returning `Err(())` exactly
when some byte in `16..32` is nonzero and `Ok(Self(value))` otherwise. The
indexing cannot panic: `bytes` has length 32.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh, and check it succeeds.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs
index c417780..f0e2199 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/scalar.rs
@@ -1429,11 +1429,14 @@ impl TryFrom<Scalar> for HalfWidthScalar {
     /// Attempt to view `scalar` as a `HalfWidthScalar`. Returns `Ok` if `value` is less
     /// than \\( 2^{128} \\)
     fn try_from(value: Scalar) -> Result<Self, Self::Error> {
-        if value.bytes[16..].iter().all(|&byte| byte == 0) {
-            Ok(Self(value))
-        } else {
-            Err(())
+        let mut i = 16;
+        while i < 32 {
+            if value.bytes[i] != 0 {
+                return Err(());
+            }
+            i += 1;
         }
+        Ok(Self(value))
     }
 }
 
